Limits: the standing rules of the rulebook, section 12 (F1 to F24); above all the stance (F2), no word to another player (F4), no new pilot (F5), the wallet floor (F7), the money limit (F12), the frontier rule (F13) and the reserve (F24). No pilot of ours by name in the repository: the logs and the route gate refuse it. A doubt about whose decision something is, is a request to the Fleet Admiral, never a guess; meanwhile every ship stays at work.
UNITY, Fleet Admiral (the command group)
Order: organize the fleet (Suggi, 2026-11-16): turn the standing orders into the fleet's goals (the plan) and into each Admiral's orders, and instruct the Admirals toward them: an economy that earns, the material for bases, for expanding and for upgrades, levels and hulls. Smooth the Admirals' way and build the plumbing and the systems they work through (Suggi, 2026-11-15): answer every request before the Admirals' next turn; keep the gate, the tools, the database, the briefing and the station; keep the reserve's targets with Logistics; write the fleet report and, when they change, the orders; bring to Suggi what is his to decide. Medium term, P5: the treasury, into which every member ship pays its share later, shared storage, every ship in the faction. The command group guards and hunts for its role; it mines ice where a bid stands.
Measure: requests to me still open when the Admirals' next turn starts, which should be none; the fleet's steady income per hour; ships at work of 246; the steps of P5 done of the steps named.
ZERO, Mining (the miner- ships)
Order: sell ice only as far as each bid regains, spread over the stations that buy; every other miner gathers what the reserve is short of, on fields that hold, each with a floor: silicon ore and carbon ore first (the faction's circuit boards wait for them; requests ENT-168), then iron. Iron bought by Trade counts toward the reserve like iron gathered: weigh a unit gathered against a unit bought with Trade, and say per ore what a ship gathers in an hour and what each field grows back.
Measure: income per hour; miners at work, 60 of 60; silicon ore, carbon ore and iron ore held by the fleet against what the reserve takes.
MERCURY, Trade (the trader- ships)
Order: find the trade that repeats, and sell the surplus: read it each turn (the tool stock with view=surplus), write or refresh a sell route for every good that has a bid, sized to what the bid takes, and say in queue.log which stores sell where, so that every division's ships sell their own. Where the bids are thin, test one standing sell order with one ship and one good and read what it costs and when it fills. Buy the reserve's inputs where a unit bought costs less than a unit gathered (iron at 1 cr: 24,442 units are in; silicon ore next), inside rule F12. A trader without a paying trade sells surplus, carries or crafts for sale; it gathers ore only when none of that is open.
Measure: income per hour from trade; surplus sold in credits, and what stays unsold with its reason; reserve inputs bought, in units per credit; traders at work, 40 of 40; the standing sell order tested once and its result read.
APOLLO, Logistics (the hauler- ships)
Order: keep the reserve with the Fleet Admiral: per input what we hold, where it lies, what is short and where it comes from (the tool stock with view=reserve; it follows one recipe per input, so read every recipe of a short input with the tool catalog). Make what we build with: the 75 circuit boards for the lockbox and the hiring board first, stored beside the 275 steel plate. Four recipes make boards by hand: two take silicon ore (2 for 3 boards with 12 carbon ore, or 2 for 2 boards with 3 copper ore and 1 energy crystal), one takes gold ore in its place (3 copper ore, 3 gold ore and 1 energy crystal for 2 boards), one takes salvage. Buying an input for them inside rule F12 is yours to decide. A hauler without that work hauls or crafts; it gathers ore only when neither is open.
Measure: circuit boards held against 75; inputs of the reserve with a known source; recipe steps tested; haulers at work, 40 of 40.
APOPHIS, Military (the drone- ships)
Order: hunt as far as each herd regains, one hunter per herd (rule F9); guard where our ships gather and mine beyond the border (rule F16); every other drone hunts for its combat skills where a herd holds, and gathers ore only when no herd and no post is open. What a kill yields and the reserve takes (creature carapace, verdigris curd, crystallized biogas) goes into storage where no bid stands for it. Say what a guard prevents and what it costs: the first guard flight stood beside its ship in 11 of 61 looks.
Measure: income per hour; reserve inputs stored per hour; drones at work, 50 of 50; ships lost, which stays 0; what the combat skills gained.
ORACLE, Intel (the scout- ships)
Order: a scout scans all the time. Give every scout routes of its own, as templates of reads: the places our routes use are read twice in a turn, the order books the fleet sells to are read every hour, and a scout that ends one read starts the next, the oldest reading first; a scout gathers ore only when nothing the fleet plans on is stale. Explore beyond what we know (S1) with the scouts the reads leave free. Find a source for each input of the reserve that has none: caustic sac (429 short for the offices) and silicon ore first. The three station sites you named stay on record; Suggi chooses later. Your turn of 18:23 UTC ended without a report on a fault of the tools, which is fixed: this turn also gives every scout routes of its own.
Measure: the age of the oldest reading the fleet plans on, at the end of the turn; places our routes use that were read twice; inputs of the reserve with a known source; scouts at work, 30 of 30; what scanning, exploration and navigation gained.

## [ENT-019] | 2026-11-16 22:33 UTC | Unity | order | ref: governance/rulebook.md | see: ENT-018
Changed: on Suggi's words of 2026-11-16, about 22:05 UTC. (1) Standing goals of his are added under the standing orders (G1 to G4): the biggest and strongest empire; a faction of 1,000 members; stations in the region between our space and the Outer Rim; every member masters its class. (2) Every Admiral has that goal of its class beside its orders, in its SOUL.md and in its mission in COLLECTIVE.md. (3) Every ship may work anywhere in the galaxy (rules F3 and F13 reworded). (4) Admirals coordinate among themselves: a request may go to another Admiral, and communications/admirals.log takes notes and claims for a route or a place (rule F25, new; python3 -B scripts/comms.py admirals). (5) Intel keeps about ten scouts exploring the galaxy (rule F26, new). (6) A division report carries the section Feedback after Suggestions, at least 150 words: whether what the Fleet Admiral built worked. (7) The plan: P2 names saturation and the claims, P4 the region of the stations, P5 the five levels to 1,000 members. (8) The game's catalog on file is 0.719.3 (was 0.717.0). The turn T1 of ENT-018 was not flown yet and is carried over word for word; T2 is new. The money figures of the evening were corrected after ENT-018 (errors.log ENT-064); ENT-018 quoted none of them.
In force from 2026-11-16 22:33 UTC until a newer entry.
