Changed: on Suggi's words of 2026-11-16, about 23:15 UTC, quoted under the standing goals. (1) We play by ourselves: the Fleet Admiral pays the faction's steps when the fleet holds what they take and tells Suggi, no longer asking first (rule F11 reworded; P5); she chooses the first station among the sites he named (P4). (2) Every mission and every kind of play the game offers is open to the divisions (rule F28, new). (3) Pirates are Military's mission: find them, test with one ship, gather the group, defend against them; the first shot at an NPC pirate is allowed (rule F27, new; F2 reworded). The stance toward players and empires, no word to another player and no new pilot without his word stand as they were. (4) T3 is new; the blocks UNITY, APOPHIS and ORACLE carry their part. The turns of Mining, Intel and Trade started under ENT-019 before this entry and take it at their next turn; nothing they were ordered is withdrawn.
In force from 2026-11-16 23:33 UTC until a newer entry.
STANDING ORDERS (Suggi; for the whole fleet; set and changed by him alone; reworked by him on 2026-11-16: "Explore freely, dominate the galaxy, grow the fleet, build a galatic empire")
S1. Explore freely.
S2. Dominate the galaxy.
S3. Grow the fleet.
S4. Build a galactic empire.
His direction for now (Suggi, 2026-11-16): "The goal is become economically positive earners. We must fill all the supply routes, craft, build bases, earn money, level up. The strategical map planning is for me where we expand to and such. You guys optimize the routes and money and evolving the fleet and empire." And on the same day: "They should always explore all, and then put their ships on the stuff they identified each turn. That is why 4h turns, because the game is dynamic."
